Cards numbered 1 to 30 are put in a bag. A card is drawn at random from this bag. Find the probability that the number on the drawn card is: not divisible by 3.
0.667
0.7
0.733
0.75
Solution:
Total cards = 30
Numbers divisible by 3 from 1 to 30: 3, 6, 9, ..., 30, which is 30 ÷ 3 = 10 cards
Numbers not divisible by 3 = 30 − 10 = 20

P(not divisible by 3) = 20/30 = 2/3 ≈ 0.667

Check using the complement: P(divisible by 3) = 10/30 = 1/3, so P(not divisible) = 1 − 1/3 = 2/3 ✓

The correct option is 0.667.
